ss margin and converts 2% of revenue into free cash flow.","Earnings quality is mixed: cash conversion of 1.81x, but a weak Piotroski score of 3/9.","ROE of 15% comes mostly from margins and asset turnover rather than leverage (3.1x equity multiplier).","It spends 0.7% of revenue on stock compensation."],"hlth":["The company holds more cash than debt."],"growth":["Revenue has compounded at 11.7% over 3 years, 12.4% over 5 years and 9.0% over 10 years.","At current returns, reinvesting 95% of profits supports about 30.0% a year of fundamental growth, enough to sustain growth.","Free cash flow has compounded -21.3% a year over five years, short of the 5% durability bar.","Capex runs 2.3x depreciation (6.6% of sales), so it is building capacity for future growth.","Its Rule of 40 score is 14, below the 40 that marks a healthy growth business.","It has beaten earnings estimates by 3.3% on average."],"own":["Insiders own a modest 4.5%, and reported institutional holdings exceed 100% of shares (a sign of heavy share lending).","Insider trading is two-way: 7 purchases and 2 sales over the past year, net $222K bought.","It returns 5.7% a year to shareholders (2.6% in buybacks and 3.3% in dividends).","It has paid a dividend for 14 consecutive years, raising it 31.0% a year over the last five.","Short interest is elevated at 23.0% of the float, 4.5 days to cover."],"people":["With about 31,600 employees, each generates about $545K of revenue, 1.4x the Consumer Cyclical median, and revenue has grown 8.8% a year across its filed history.","That works out to $13K of free cash flow per employee.","CEO pay is $3.9M (7x revenue per employee), and compensation governance scores well (2/10, lower is better).","Stock compensation averages $4K per employee."]},"profile":{"v":"INVEST","conv":76,"head":"Invest: trades 17% below fair value of $181; ROIC 97.3% vs WACC 9.9%.","pros":["Composite 54, above the 39 line (gates 15/26)","Trades 17% below fair value of $181","ROIC 97.3% vs WACC 9